From d27758f82110cedd0e0b82db892e35d090383439 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ivory <contact@ivory.cafe>
Date: Tue, 1 Sep 2026 19:27:49 +0800
Subject: [PATCH 07/32] Give Manager an explicit namespace walk control

Persist and validate the namespace prefix used to target DexCache-backed class discovery, expose it in Advanced settings, and keep the schema and tests aligned with Framework and ART.

Constraint: Preserve exhaustive configuration serialization and fail-closed validation.
Rejected: Reusing force_class as an implicit namespace selector | It conflates exact method selection with discovery scope.
Confidence: high
Scope-risk: moderate
Directive: Keep namespace prefixes segment-bounded and retain the trailing dot invariant.
Tested: r0dump_f7_class_loader_walk_source_test.py; r0dump_config_boundary_source_test.py; git diff --check.
Not-tested: Full Manager/AOSP build; lunch release configuration is unavailable in this checkout.
